{
  "version": 3,
  "about": "Single source of truth for what the document sandbox image ships. The Dockerfile installs every python[].pip from this file (binary wheels; sdist only for the pure-Python names in python_sdist_ok), downloads the data in python_data, and fails the build when an import or a cli[] binary is missing (verify_env.py) or when the pytest suite in tests/ (one functional test per entry, enforced by test_zz_catalog_coverage.py) fails. backend/src/services/agent-runner/sandbox-capabilities.json is a byte-identical copy the agent prompt is built from (a test enforces it). Compiled extensions must be regular cp312 wheels: abi3 wheels built with Cython's limited API (cftime>=1.6.6, netCDF4>=1.7.3, astropy>=7.2) register a Cython shared type of a different size and crash every later import ('Shared Cython type cython_function_or_method has the wrong size'); their pins stay below those releases. numpy stays below 2.4 (np.in1d and other 2.0-deprecated names were removed there) so astropy 7.1, the last release with regular cp312 wheels, keeps working.",
